MRP System Frontend – Comprehensive Audit & Fix Status Report
Date: 2026-03-28
Branch: refactor/data-layer-cleanup
Scope: All codebase issues identified in the 10 original audits, with status after our refactoring and subsequent fixes.

1. Executive Summary
Since the initial audits, we have made significant progress in code quality, performance, and accessibility, raising the overall project score from 2.2/10 to 3.7/10. The following areas saw the biggest improvements:

React Patterns & Architecture: Added hooks, global error boundary, skip‑to‑main link, document.title updates, and vendor chunk splitting.

API & Services: Enhanced HTTP status handling, removed many console.logs, and fixed the BOM modal contract.

DevOps: Introduced pre‑commit hooks (husky + lint‑staged) to enforce quality.

Accessibility: Added skip link and dynamic page titles.

Performance: Added vendor chunk splitting and ensured useFetch supports abort and tab visibility.

However, critical gaps remain:

No authentication or route protection – the app is open to anyone.

Type safety – strict: false and many any types still in services.

Security – dependency vulnerabilities (xlsx), hardcoded URLs.

Testing – zero test infrastructure.

Material Tailwind – still used in 17 files; must be fully removed.

The following report details every finding from the original audits, with updated statuses.

