6. Next Steps – Prioritized for Future Work
Tier 1 – Critical (Must Fix ASAP)
Authentication & Route Protection – Implement Supabase Auth, protect all API calls and pages.

Fix Dependency Vulnerabilities – Replace xlsx with a maintained alternative; downgrade React to stable 18.3.1.

Remove @material-tailwind – Migrate remaining 17 files to custom components.

Tier 2 – High Impact
Enable strict: true and eliminate any in services.

Implement client‑side data cache – Add React Query (TanStack Query).

Add code splitting – Lazy‑load pages with React.lazy.

Complete service layer cleanup – Consolidate BOM/dashboard services, remove hardcoded URLs, delete dead code.

Tier 3 – Quality & Testing
Set up testing – Vitest + React Testing Library; write unit tests for critical logic.

Accessibility – Address WCAG 2.1 AA findings (74 items) – focus traps, form labels, etc.

Add CI/CD pipeline – GitHub Actions to run lint, test, build.

7. Conclusion
We have successfully improved the codebase’s structure, developer experience, and baseline performance. However, the project still lacks foundational security, testing, and type safety that are mandatory for an enterprise‑grade application. The next phase should prioritise authentication, dependency remediation, and the removal of the remaining Material Tailwind components.

